{
  "participants": [
    {
      "login": "pablomartin4btc",
      "stance": "support",
      "note": "Concept ACK: necessary to support private transaction broadcast mechanism when rebroadcasting"
    },
    {
      "login": "w0xlt",
      "stance": "support",
      "note": "raised concern about lack of per-transaction tracking if restarted without -privatebroadcast, but agreed to keep it simple and ACKed"
    },
    {
      "login": "mzumsande",
      "stance": "objection",
      "note": "argues PR is incomplete unless IsMine() dust transactions are also addressed"
    },
    {
      "login": "andrewtoth",
      "stance": "support",
      "note": "ACKed and pointed out #34707 could address the CPFP rebroadcast issue"
    },
    {
      "login": "achow101",
      "stance": "objection",
      "note": "not convinced PR is ready without package private broadcast support; dependent transactions (e.g., CPFP) can be delayed or fail indefinitely"
    },
    {
      "login": "sedited",
      "stance": "neutral",
      "note": "asked whether the PR should be marked draft while dependent issues are addressed"
    },
    {
      "login": "instagibbs",
      "stance": "neutral",
      "note": "noted package relay support limits (1P1C) for fixing dependent broadcast"
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "c:3866155658",
      "kind": "approach",
      "harm": "privately broadcast transactions could later be rebroadcast publicly via mempool if node restarts without -privatebroadcast",
      "quote": "if a user uses `sendrawtransaction` to submit a wallet-related transaction while `-privatebroadcast` is enabled and then restarts the node without `-privatebroadcast`, the transaction would be rebroadcast via mempool since there is no per-transaction tracking of how it was originally sent.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "author_replies": [
        "c:3896028216"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": false,
      "settled_by_id": "r:3829186494",
      "settled_by_quote": "However, it’s probably better to keep things simple. ACK 16cd713073f45a5ddff1cdce73a7a8459bd8c618"
    },
    {
      "id": "r:3790883774",
      "kind": "scope",
      "harm": "an attacker can send dust to wallet addresses to trigger public rebroadcasts unless IsMine transactions are also handled",
      "quote": "I think this is not complete unless we also do something about `IsMine()` transactions.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "open",
      "author_replies": [],
      "fix_pushed": false,
      "settled_by_id": "",
      "settled_by_quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "c:3969991481",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "harm": "private broadcast to random peers fails or indefinitely delays rebroadcasting dependent transactions (e.g. CPFP) because parent is missing from local mempool",
      "quote": "I'm not convinced that this is ready for the wallet until there is support for private broadcasting of packages, and for the wallet to submit packages when rebroadcasting.",
      "blocking": true,
      "status": "open",
      "author_replies": [
        "c:3998092851"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": false,
      "settled_by_id": "",
      "settled_by_quote": ""
    }
  ],
  "support": [
    {
      "id": "r:3767548873",
      "verdict": "Concept ACK",
      "reason": "This is necessary to support the private transaction broadcast mechanism introduced in #29415 when transactions are rebroadcast or resubmitted, which does not seem to be handled currently.",
      "substantive": true
    },
    {
      "id": "r:3829186494",
      "verdict": "ACK",
      "reason": "Agreed keeping it simple without per-transaction state complexity is better: 'ACK 16cd713073f45a5ddff1cdce73a7a8459bd8c618'",
      "substantive": true
    },
    {
      "id": "r:3851369970",
      "verdict": "ACK",
      "reason": "ACK 16cd713073f45a5ddff1cdce73a7a8459bd8c618",
      "substantive": false
    }
  ],
  "notes": "achow101 raised a blocking concern regarding rebroadcast of dependent transactions / CPFP without package private broadcast support, which vasild acknowledged as an issue. mzumsande also raised an open scope concern regarding IsMine() transactions."
}
